{
  "abstract": "Formalizes the core tensoriality behavior of the raw curvature commutator for covariant derivatives on smooth finite-dimensional manifolds. The selected results prove pointwise scalar linearity in the left tangent-field slot, the middle tangent-field slot, and the bundle-section slot, together with skew-adjointness of the curvature commutator under metric compatibility. These are standard differential-geometric identities; the contribution claimed here is their kernel-checked formalization with the regularity hypotheses exposed at the Mathlib manifold/vector-bundle API boundary, not a new discovery or a priority claim. The implementation also contains the resulting bundled curvature and Ricci/scalar contraction infrastructure, which is outside this selected surface.",
